<title>KUWAIT: Kuwait T-bill balance falls in April yr/yr.</title>
<headline>Kuwait T-bill balance falls in April yr/yr.</headline>
<dateline>KUWAIT 1997-06-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>The outstanding balance of treasury bills issued by Kuwait's Central Bank fell to 1.168 billion dinars at the end of April from 1.412 million in the same period of 1996, a Central Bank bulletin said.</p>
<p>They rose from 1.149 million in March 1997.</p>
<p>The outstanding balance of public debt instruments -- bonds and bills -- fell to 2.434 billion dinars at the end of April from 2.456 billion at the end of March.</p>
<p>The balance of public debt instruments was 2.701 billion in April 1996.</p>
<p>				 Data in million dinars</p>
<p>			April '97    March '97     April '96</p>
<p>Bills</p>
<p>  Matured	     250.0	  226.4	   727.4</p>
<p>  New Issue	   269.5	  206.9	   449.0</p>
<p>  Balance	   1,168.3	1,148.8	 1,412.0</p>
<p>Bonds</p>
<p>  Matured	     230.0	  250.0	     --</p>
<p>  New Issue	   188.4	  230.0	   230.0</p>
<p>  Balance	   1,265.4	1,307.0	 1,280.9</p>
<p>Slight discrepancies in figures are due to rounding.</p>
